{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-42813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:=-4{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let  $E=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=3{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad