field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{2}:=-5{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of the identity matrix by $-10$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation  ${R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-130839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:=10{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+(-10){R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-10){R}_{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=18{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=18{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=18{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-130853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130845" "field" nil "attribute" "que