\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-130852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-130847" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130847" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130847" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-32037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-32037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations. \n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-c