hen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-130860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9814f4a50ae065ff0445b5d3e2eac15b0c30e0d777627cdd25265d2451ba5c32"} {"question" "q-130859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "q-130859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ed986bac74899e8028869cf48c173abd4f261de39e3b88a3303a9d660e75927"} {"question" "e-4720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/38c4cba166fdfcd0954a18156946e41834a626cccee4baab976861dd23574c85.png) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/example-4720.json" "file_sha256" "dd273f4598f4a52f05bce67daac6d1bca639f29eadf50ce9f5ca093c3b80b9be"} {"question" "e-4720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/example-4720.json" "file_sha256" "dd273f4598f4a52f05bce67daac6d1bca639f29eadf50ce9f5ca093c3b80b9be"} {"question" "e-4721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/example-4721.json" "file_sha256" "7f5fa0f4f13bac157d180dd0aa3f256b8f659e6c8d46048a4def239902418c30"} {"question" "e-4721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/a4a2b1035b3b5699ff3558ffa839fbd667ad6defaf30a158d628c7011ab97aa8.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/example-4721.json" "file_sha256" "7f5fa0f4f13bac157d180dd0aa3f256b8f659e6c8d46048a4def239902418c30"} {"question" "e-4722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/example-4722.json" "file_sha256" "48dc9bfa1658fd17a377fe8ba836f26ba90f98301e4914ef76c113960c210823"} {"question" "e-4722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/d35cb368b7380f08e486757813138fa3f3332ed40a9b0e5faeab7a20c3119bef.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/c87dbe6c81a670dd62d8a130d3085b2e9b36d5d3ad27d53bda571ec69b639689.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/example-4722.json" "file_sha256" "48dc9bfa1658fd17a377fe8ba836f26ba90f98301e4914ef76c113960c210823"} {"question" "q-42767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "a165dcb7636a6637d2599c67fd248cbd9f55da0f491a178c3bd85327b4d06a07" "reviewer_session" "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca" "rationale" "The three operations correspond to E1=[[1,0],[0,-2]], E2=[[0,1],[1,0]], and E3=[[1,0],[3,1]]. Successive row operations multiply on the left, giving E3E2E1A, exactly original option 3 and the stored answer. Their composite matrix is [[0,-2],[1,-6]]. Preserve multiplication order. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the original operations and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns submitted option 4, not this reviewed answer." "bindings" {"problem" "c19fb58bfe3920240c0097dd708754eb5ea3397317d6b2b1e57ebf68fca36245" "worked_solution" "603c9a51d89b49204d60f9d9da34c9729b1c7254a054cbf225edab8120b4e56e" "original_field" "ced2b0b94a20f04d34b8922cbf1f60724c70f0a2a65f8d65fc09a89fb34a7777" "reviewed_field" "b40fe2d583e8e59ad7ec751fa6990cb7d8468e44d1a8a41a9e703e16728f5e4c" "raw_widget" "153a09a1c7c650d1ac602a90eb550319830aa3e3c6ec64cfb287bebd6bad3d3d"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-42767-before.png" "sha256" "0b7b8be9473752d103f06ecb90e7caa44aaf381ba668ca8374a5f5a700d7e2a7"} {"path" "history-q-42767.png" "sha256" "8b6875630a8fa0b070ec46289c4daebf923d30a212e38de0422599141c724e94"} {"path" "q-42767-after.json" "sha256" "67a1b13a9cbd492577b8cfae4d7d5da37989a9abfe1055a87759eae0c10e50c2"}]} {"question" "q-42767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" 